WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:36.875
<b>Lord Krishna explained that</b>
<b>desire is humanity's eternal enemy.</b>

2
00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:42.916
<b>Here, Krishna reveals where </b>
<b>this enemy can be found.</b>

3
00:00:47.458 --> 00:00:54.125
<b>Krishna teaches that desire influences </b>
<b>our senses, mind, and intellect –		</b>

4
00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:59.125
<b>these three places are where desire resides.</b>

5
00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:08.291
<b>By controlling our senses, mind, and intellect, </b>
<b>desire completely veils our true wisdom.</b>

6
00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:12.791
<b>The text uses the word "vimohaiti,"</b>

7
00:01:12.791 --> 00:01:16.375
<b>"vimohaiti,"meaning to become deluded,</b>

8
00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.708
<b>and this is precisely what happens.</b>

9
00:01:18.708 --> 00:01:23.708
<b>Instead of understanding its true nature, </b>
<b>the soul becomes confused</b>

10
00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:29.208
<b>and is drawn toward worldly pleasures.</b>

11
00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:30.125
<b>But</b>

12
00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:37.833
<b>what does it mean when we say </b>
<b>desire dwells in these three places?</b>

13
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:45.083
<b>It means that first, our senses perceive </b>
<b>and become attracted to an object.</b>

14
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:49.333
<b>Then, the mind develops wishes</b>
<b>to experience that object,</b>

15
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:54.166
<b>and finally, the intellect plans </b>
<b>how to fulfill these wishes.</b>

16
00:01:54.166 --> 00:01:59.500
<b>In this way, the soul becomes completely</b>
<b>entangled in sensual tendencies.</b>

17
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:04.208
<b>Desire doesn't exist in objects – it exists within us.</b>

18
00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:10.291
<b>Often, people become lustful seeing </b>
<b>someone's beauty or body,</b>

19
00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:17.041
<b>but if the same form is seen by a child, </b>
<b>they feel no such desire.</b>

20
00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:18.791
<b>Why is this?</b>

21
00:02:18.791 --> 00:02:26.458
<b>Because desire isn't in what we see, </b>
<b>but within ourselves.</b>

22
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:33.041
<b>The purpose of our values and culture is </b>
<b>to elevate our consciousness</b>

23
00:02:33.041 --> 00:02:35.708
<b>and enable spiritual growth.</b>

24
00:02:35.708 --> 00:02:40.958
<b>However, if we make this physical </b>
<b>body the center of our culture,</b>

25
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:48.375
<b>it will push us toward sensual indulgence </b>
<b>rather than spiritual elevation.</b>

26
00:02:48.375 --> 00:02:51.458
<b>Ancient culture was consciousness-based,</b>

27
00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:52.416
<b>but</b>

28
00:02:52.416 --> 00:02:58.958
<b>modern culture is gradually becoming centered</b>
<b>on materialism and pleasure.</b>

29
00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:04.125
<b>Which culture we lean toward is a crucial choice,</b>

30
00:03:04.125 --> 00:03:11.708
<b>as this determines whether we'll ultimately </b>
<b>find liberation or remain in bondage.</b>

31
00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:17.916
<b>Material culture focuses solely on</b>
<b>personal sensual gratification.</b>

32
00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:20.791
<b>In such cases, people often assume</b>

33
00:03:20.791 --> 00:03:26.291
<b>they can live however they </b>
<b>please without regard for others.</b>

34
00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:30.250
<b>They believe that as long as no one is watching,</b>

35
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.375
<b>they can do anything for physical pleasure.</b>

36
00:03:34.375 --> 00:03:36.416
<b>And in the name of modernity,</b>

37
00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:39.541
<b>this mindset promotes desire,</b>

38
00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:45.708
<b>diminishes our wisdom, and leads </b>
<b>to suffering in this world.</b>

39
00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:49.833
<b>While desire may seem</b>
<b>pleasurable for a brief time,</b>

40
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:54.125
<b>ultimately, when it blazes like fire,</b>

41
00:03:54.125 --> 00:03:59.291
<b>it brings nothing but misery to humankind.</b>

42
00:04:03.833 --> 00:04:06.000
<b>Consider,</b>

43
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.833
<b>for our desires and temptations,</b>

44
00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:16.708
<b>how easy it is to blame external </b>
<b>circumstances or others.</b>

45
00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:22.833
<b>We think if only the world </b>
<b>around us was different – </b>

46
00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:26.333
<b>less tempting, less challenging –</b>

47
00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:31.000
<b>we wouldn't have to struggle with these desires.</b>

48
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.833
<b>But</b>

49
00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:39.708
<b>in truth, the battle with desire is internal.</b>

50
00:04:39.708 --> 00:04:45.666
<b>If an object or person draws us toward lust,</b>

51
00:04:45.666 --> 00:04:50.250
<b>it merely reflects our inner state.</b>

52
00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:59.083
<b>It's like someone with diabetes </b>
<b>who starts eating sweets</b>

53
00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:00.125
<b>and then</b>

54
00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:10.916
<b>blames the candy shop for their inability </b>
<b>to control their diet and health.</b>

55
00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:13.916
<b>Though the shop may offer </b>
<b>countless temptations,</b>

56
00:05:13.916 --> 00:05:15.125
<b>but</b>

57
00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:21.666
<b>it isn't the root cause of that </b>
<b>person's craving for sweets;</b>

58
00:05:21.666 --> 00:05:27.458
<b>that craving exists independently within them,</b>

59
00:05:27.458 --> 00:05:31.375
<b>and if that shop didn't exist,</b>

60
00:05:31.375 --> 00:05:36.833
<b>the craving would find another outlet.</b>

61
00:05:36.833 --> 00:05:38.250
<b>Understanding</b>

62
00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.458
<b>that desire originates from within</b>

63
00:05:41.458 --> 00:05:43.875
<b>is accepting</b>

64
00:05:43.875 --> 00:05:51.125
<b>that we have both the power and</b>
<b>responsibility to control it.</b>

65
00:05:51.125 --> 00:05:58.833
<b>Rather than expending energy trying </b>
<b>to change or avoid external causes,</b>

66
00:05:58.833 --> 00:06:07.166
<b>we must focus on strengthening </b>
<b>our inner resolve and self-discipline.</b>

67
00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:11.916
<b>This requires deep self-reflection:</b>

68
00:06:11.916 --> 00:06:16.791
<b>Why do certain things affect us so profoundly?</b>

69
00:06:16.791 --> 00:06:26.666
<b>What is it within us that's so intensely </b>
<b>drawn to these external objects?</b>

70
00:06:26.666 --> 00:06:31.541
<b>Regular meditation and </b>
<b>time spent in self-observation</b>

71
00:06:31.541 --> 00:06:35.250
<b>will protect us from the longing </b>
<b>for immediate pleasures,</b>

72
00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:41.541
<b>steering us toward contentment </b>
<b>and purposeful goals.</b>

73
00:06:41.541 --> 00:06:43.125
<b>Ultimately,</b>

74
00:06:43.125 --> 00:06:46.125
<b>when we accept </b>

75
00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:51.625
<b>that desire resides not in the </b>
<b>external world but within us,</b>

76
00:06:51.625 --> 00:06:58.541
<b>we become capable of controlling </b>
<b>our actions and emotions.</b>

77
00:06:58.541 --> 00:07:06.458
<b>In this light, you can view situations full </b>
<b>of temptation as spiritual opportunities.</b>

78
00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:09.208
<b>By rejecting worldly temptations,</b>

79
00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:15.083
<b>you can strengthen your spiritual power.</b>

80
00:07:15.083 --> 00:07:16.583
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

81
00:07:16.583 --> 00:07:19.750
<b>Don't get caught in temptations.</b>

82
00:07:24.375 --> 00:07:29.208
<b>Think of your family as a garden.</b>

83
00:07:29.208 --> 00:07:35.666
<b>A garden where every experience </b>
<b>that comes through the senses</b>

84
00:07:35.666 --> 00:07:37.583
<b>is like a seed</b>

85
00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:40.625
<b>that will ultimately grow.</b>

86
00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:44.708
<b>This sensory contact can come from anything –</b>

87
00:07:44.708 --> 00:07:48.791
<b>what you see, hear, understand –</b>

88
00:07:48.791 --> 00:07:50.208
<b>anything.</b>

89
00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:51.791
<b>And these seeds,</b>

90
00:07:51.791 --> 00:07:53.000
<b>these experiences,</b>

91
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:59.750
<b>will determine how our family garden develops.</b>

92
00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:08.791
<b>Are we sowing seeds that promote material </b>
<b>desires and personal indulgence,</b>

93
00:08:08.791 --> 00:08:19.208
<b>or are we planting seeds of life values </b>
<b>that foster spiritual growth and self-discipline?</b>

94
00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:21.375
<b>Today, in every family,</b>

95
00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:22.333
<b>TV,</b>

96
00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:25.000
<b>computers, and through other media,</b>

97
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:31.041
<b>countless colorful programs </b>
<b>are available at all times.</b>

98
00:08:31.041 --> 00:08:39.750
<b>Hundreds of these programs only promote </b>
<b>momentary pleasure and sensual gratification.</b>

99
00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:48.125
<b>Such programs can unknowingly </b>
<b>influence our desires and behavior.</b>

100
00:08:48.125 --> 00:08:49.666
<b>For instance,</b>

101
00:08:49.666 --> 00:08:55.625
<b>if a family regularly watches programs</b>

102
00:08:55.625 --> 00:09:04.041
<b>where characters only live with expensive </b>
<b>cars, costly clothes, and lives of luxury,</b>

103
00:09:04.041 --> 00:09:10.833
<b>it will awaken the desire for such </b>
<b>a lifestyle in the family members.</b>

104
00:09:10.833 --> 00:09:18.875
<b>They'll begin to think this is </b>
<b>how normal life should be.</b>

105
00:09:18.875 --> 00:09:20.625
<b>Is this right?</b>

106
00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:24.666
<b>It's essential to ask ourselves:</b>

107
00:09:24.666 --> 00:09:32.458
<b>What influences are we allowing to</b>
<b>affect our senses, mind, and intellect?</b>

108
00:09:32.458 --> 00:09:38.833
<b>Do these influences help reduce desire</b>
<b>and material attachment,</b>

109
00:09:38.833 --> 00:09:43.583
<b>or are they entangling us further?</b>

110
00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:50.541
<b>This isn't about restriction, nor about protecting</b>
<b>your family from the outside world.</b>

111
00:09:50.541 --> 00:09:53.875
<b>It's about making the right choices.</b>

112
00:09:53.875 --> 00:10:02.583
<b>It's about being aware of what kind of</b>
<b>life values we want to develop in our family,</b>

113
00:10:02.583 --> 00:10:11.041
<b>and accordingly, what types of programs </b>
<b>and experiences will support this path.</b>

114
00:10:11.041 --> 00:10:16.000
<b>If you want to develop values in your family</b>

115
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:24.166
<b>that reduce material desires and.</b>
<b>promote meaningful life principles,</b>

116
00:10:24.166 --> 00:10:28.291
<b>here are some measures you can take:</b>

117
00:10:28.291 --> 00:10:29.375
<b>First -</b>

118
00:10:29.375 --> 00:10:32.458
<b>Choose proper entertainment:</b>

119
00:10:32.458 --> 00:10:39.250
<b>Select programs that help </b>
<b>maintain family values.</b>

120
00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.666
<b>Second -</b>

121
00:10:40.666 --> 00:10:42.708
<b>Family time:</b>

122
00:10:42.708 --> 00:10:46.750
<b>Set aside time each day where </b>
<b>the family sits together,</b>

123
00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.500
<b>talks,</b>

124
00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.125
<b>discusses daily routines.</b>

125
00:10:51.125 --> 00:10:53.333
<b>No programs, </b>

126
00:10:53.333 --> 00:10:54.583
<b>no phones,</b>

127
00:10:54.583 --> 00:10:56.333
<b>no television.</b>

128
00:10:56.333 --> 00:10:58.041
<b>And the third,</b>

129
00:10:58.041 --> 00:11:00.541
<b>Spiritual education:</b>

130
00:11:00.541 --> 00:11:06.333
<b>Choose programs and books </b>
<b>that while being entertaining,</b>

131
00:11:06.333 --> 00:11:08.000
<b>teach morality,</b>

132
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.708
<b>self-control,</b>

133
00:11:09.708 --> 00:11:12.916
<b>and encourage spiritual messages.</b>

134
00:11:12.916 --> 00:11:16.333
<b>Taking such positive steps in the family,</b>

135
00:11:16.333 --> 00:11:18.875
<b>selecting the right experiences,</b>

136
00:11:18.875 --> 00:11:25.083
<b>not only reflects our family </b>
<b>values but by doing so,</b>

137
00:11:25.083 --> 00:11:32.708
<b>we're also promoting a culture that </b>
<b>protects us from material desires</b>

138
00:11:32.708 --> 00:11:39.750
<b>and helps us recognize our true spiritual nature.</b>

139
00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.416
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

140
00:11:46.833 --> 00:11:49.958
<b>In today's modern workplaces, </b>

141
00:11:49.958 --> 00:11:54.458
<b>there are numerous opportunities</b>
<b>for sensual temptation</b>

142
00:11:54.458 --> 00:11:59.041
<b>whether it's financial gain, </b>
<b>promotion opportunities,</b>

143
00:11:59.041 --> 00:12:00.208
<b>or</b>

144
00:12:00.208 --> 00:12:04.166
<b>personal relationships with others.</b>

145
00:12:04.166 --> 00:12:08.541
<b>In such circumstances, it's no surprise</b>

146
00:12:08.541 --> 00:12:15.000
<b>that some people become eager to </b>
<b>cross their professional boundaries.</b>

147
00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.708
<b>Driven by financial greed, position attachment,</b>

148
00:12:17.708 --> 00:12:24.000
<b>or personal attraction,</b>
<b>they commit unethical acts.</b>

149
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.875
<b>And when such situations arise,</b>

150
00:12:26.875 --> 00:12:30.916
<b>people never blame themselves –</b>

151
00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:37.875
<b>they justify their unethical behavior</b>
<b>by saying things like</b>

152
00:12:37.875 --> 00:12:44.208
<b>'others are doing it too' or 'this is normal,'</b>

153
00:12:44.208 --> 00:12:45.750
<b>but</b>

154
00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:48.375
<b>the Gita teaches –</b>

155
00:12:48.375 --> 00:12:49.583
<b>that desire</b>

156
00:12:49.583 --> 00:12:53.708
<b>and attraction towards unethical </b>
<b>behavior's true cause</b>

157
00:12:53.708 --> 00:13:00.083
<b>isn't in any external object</b>
<b>or person, but within us.</b>

158
00:13:00.083 --> 00:13:03.916
<b>No one else can be blamed for this.</b>

159
00:13:03.916 --> 00:13:05.583
<b>To avoid this,</b>

160
00:13:05.583 --> 00:13:08.083
<b>if anything can be done,</b>

161
00:13:08.083 --> 00:13:17.250
<b>it's first to accept that protecting ourselves from </b>
<b>these temptations is our responsibility,</b>

162
00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:22.666
<b>and to do so, we must look within</b>

163
00:13:22.666 --> 00:13:25.208
<b>and correct our mistakes.</b>

164
00:13:25.208 --> 00:13:31.166
<b>And for this, it's necessary that we </b>
<b>become spiritually strong.</b>

165
00:13:31.166 --> 00:13:34.833
<b>This will not only protect us</b>
<b>from unethical behavior</b>

166
00:13:34.833 --> 00:13:42.458
<b>but will also help us make </b>
<b>our work standards the highest.</b>

167
00:13:42.458 --> 00:13:44.541
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

